Each case converts the internationalized domain names of input to punycode by ToASCII,
output is the converted list, or error is a part of the error message.
-- input --
例子.com
full:münchen.de @de
日本.jp &asia
faß.de
ドメイン名例.jp
مثال.إختبار
example.com
xn--fsqu00a.例子.com
-- output --
xn--fsqu00a.com
full:xn--mnchen-3ya.de @de
xn--wgv71a.jp &asia
xn--fa-hia.de
xn--eckwd4c7cu47r2wf.jp
xn--mgbh0fb.xn--kgbechtv
example.com
xn--fsqu00a.xn--fsqu00a.com
-- input --
# Names are mapped by UTS #46, the fullwidth and the ideographic full stop.
ｅｘａｍｐｌｅ.com
例子。com
-- output --
example.com
xn--fsqu00a.com
-- input --
# Keywords and regexps are kept as is, a part of a label could not be converted alone.
keyword:例子
regexp:^例子\.com$
-- output --
keyword:例子
regexp:^例子\.com$
-- input --
# ASCII names are kept as is, even the invalid ones.
example..com
-- output --
example..com
-- input --
例子.com
-例子.com
-- error --
domains[1]: invalid domain "-例子.com": idna: invalid label "-例子"
